// The Lance -- four sounds, namespaced so this drops into any mod without
// colliding with its sound names.
//
// lnc/loop is the one that matters: it is started with CHANF_LOOPING when the
// trigger goes down and pitched every tic after, so the approaching cook-off
// is audible before it is visible. Each hand loops on its own high channel
// (lance.zs LOOP_CHAN_MAIN / LOOP_CHAN_OFF). It used to share CHAN_5 -- which
// is the engine's CHAN_OFFWEAPON -- so it fought the offhand's own sounds and
// the two hands fought each other.

lnc/charge    PLCHRG
// THE BEAM VOICE. Cut from the sustain body of a Klingon disruptor (0.13-0.59s
// of the source, past the attack and before the decay), then the end crossfaded
// back over the head so the wrap has no seam. 0.46s, mono, no leading silence.
//
// TWO THINGS THAT MADE EARLIER ATTEMPTS TICK, both worth knowing:
//   - ffmpeg -ss seeking INTO an mp3 primes the decoder and leaves ~20ms of
//     near-silence at the head. Decode the whole file first, then atrim.
//   - alimiter pads the stream start with its lookahead, same symptom.
// Either one puts a hole at the top of the loop that clicks every 0.46s.
lnc/loop      LNCLOOP
lnc/cookoff   PLCOUT
lnc/empty     AKEMPT
lnc/sizzle    AKEMPT

// ---- burning deaths -------------------------------------------------
//
// TWO $random GROUPS, THREE TAKES EACH, and the pyre rolls which group as
// well as letting the engine roll within it -- so six distinct screams,
// picked twice over, plus a per-play pitch shift of +/-12%. A room of
// burning zombies is a chorus instead of one sound played six times.
$random lnc/burn/scream1 { lnc/burn/zob1 lnc/burn/zob2 lnc/burn/zob3 }
$random lnc/burn/scream2 { lnc/burn/zom1 lnc/burn/zom2 lnc/burn/zom3 }

lnc/burn/zob1   BURNZOB1
lnc/burn/zob2   BURNZOB2
lnc/burn/zob3   BURNZOB3
lnc/burn/zom1   BURNZOM1
lnc/burn/zom2   BURNZOM2
lnc/burn/zom3   BURNZOM3

// The crackle under it all, looped on CHAN_BODY for the pyre's lifetime
// and stopped explicitly when it burns out.
lnc/burn/loop   DSFLAME
